          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1 The Hahn–Banach Theorems. Introduction to the Theory of Conjugate Convex Functions"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.281,
            0.073,
            0.714,
            0.309
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 2,
              "bbox": [
                0.281,
                0.073,
                0.714,
                0.309
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_20_image_2.jpg",
              "content": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "image_caption",
              "index": 3,
              "bbox": [
                0.102,
                0.319,
                0.156,
                0.335
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Fig. 1"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.103,
            0.367,
            0.649,
            0.387
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_20_equation_4.jpg",
          "content": "p ( x ) = \\operatorname* { i n f } \\{ \\alpha > 0 ; \\alpha ^ { - 1 } x \\in C \\}\\tag{8}"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.102,
            0.403,
            0.698,
            0.421
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(p is called the gauge of C or the Minkowski functional of C)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.129,
            0.43,
            0.656,
            0.449
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Then p satisfies (1), (2), and the following properties:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.102,
            0.464,
            0.79,
            0.483
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(9) there is a constant M such that "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "0 \\leq p ( x ) \\leq M \\| x \\| \\quad \\forall x \\in E"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.104,
            0.488,
            0.622,
            0.505
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_20_equation_8.jpg",
          "content": "C = \\{ x \\in E   ;   p ( x ) < 1 \\} .\\tag{10}"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.101,
            0.521,
            0.565,
            0.539
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Proof of Lemma 1.2. It is obvious that (1) holds."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.101,
            0.549,
            0.731,
            0.567
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Proof of (9). Let "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "r > 0"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " be such that "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "B ( 0 , r ) \\subset C ;"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " ; we clearly have"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.377,
            0.58,
            0.62,
            0.617
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_20_equation_11.jpg",
          "content": "p ( x ) \\leq { \\frac { 1 } { r } } \\| x \\| \\quad \\forall x \\in E ."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.1,
            0.628,
            0.897,
            0.783
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Proof of (10). First, suppose that "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "x \\in C ;"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " since C is open, it follows that "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "( 1   +   \\varepsilon ) x \\in C"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " for "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\varepsilon   >   0"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " small enough and therefore "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\textstyle p ( x )   \\leq   { \\frac { 1 } { 1 + \\varepsilon } }   <   1"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . Conversely, if "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "p ( x )   <   1"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " there exists "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\alpha \\in ( 0 , 1 )"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " such that "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\alpha ^ { - 1 } x \\in C"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , and thus "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "x = \\alpha ( \\alpha ^ { - 1 } x ) + ( 1 - \\alpha ) 0 \\in C"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Proof of(2). Let "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "x , y \\in E"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and let "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\varepsilon > 0"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . Using (1) and (10) we obtain that "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\scriptstyle { \\frac { x } { p ( x ) + \\varepsilon } } \\in C"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\scriptstyle { \\frac { y } { p ( y ) + \\varepsilon } } \\; \\in \\; C"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . Thus "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\begin{array} { r } { \\frac { t x } { p ( x ) + \\varepsilon } + \\frac { ( 1 - t ) y } { p ( y ) + \\varepsilon } \\in C } \\end{array}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " for all "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "t \\in [ 0 , 1 ]"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . Choosing the value "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\begin{array} { r } { t = \\frac { p ( x ) + \\varepsilon } { p ( x ) + p ( y ) + 2 \\varepsilon } } \\end{array}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , we find that "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac{x + y}{p(x) + p(y) + 2\\varepsilon} \\in C"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . Using (1) and (10) once more, we are led to "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "p(x+y)<p(x)+p(y)+2\\varepsilon,\\forall\\varepsilon>0"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.1,
            0.792,
            0.896,
            0.847
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Lemma 1.3. Let "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "C \\subset E"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " be a nonempty open convex set and let "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "x _ { 0 } \\in E"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " with x0 "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\notin C ."
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Then there exists "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "f \\in E ^ { \\star }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " such that "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "f ( x ) \\; < \\; f ( x _ { 0 } ) \\quad \\forall x \\; \\in \\; C"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . In particular, the hyperplane "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "[ f = f ( x _ { 0 } ) ]"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " separates {x"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "0",
              "styles": [
                "subscript"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "} and C."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.1,
            0.856,
            0.898,
            0.912
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Proof of Lemma 1.3. After a translation we may always assume that "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "0   \\in   C"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . We may thus introduce the gauge p of C (see Lemma 1.2). Consider the linear subspace "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "G = \\mathbb { R } x _ { 0 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and the linear functional "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "g : G \\to \\mathbb { R }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " defined by"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
